<title>USA: Top 10 movies at U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>Top 10 movies at U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the U.S. box office for the May 2-4 weekend, according to studio estimates collected Sunday by Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc. Final results will be issued on Monday.</p>
<p>    1 (*) Breakdown ..................... $12.7 million</p>
<p>2 (*) Austin Powers:</p>
<p>	    International Man of Mystery .. $10.0 million</p>
<p>    3 (1) Volcano .......................  $9.5 million</p>
<p>    4 (4) Liar Liar .....................  $5.8 million</p>
<p>5 (2) Romy and Michele's High</p>
<p>	    School Reunion ................  $5.6 million</p>
<p>    6 (3) Anaconda ......................  $5.0 million</p>
<p>    7 (*) Warriors of Virtue ............  $3.6 million</p>
<p>    8 (5) The Saint .....................  $3.2 million</p>
<p>    9 (6) Murder At 1600 ................  $3.0 million</p>
<p>    10(7) Grosse Pointe Blank ...........  $2.0 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Last weekend's position in parenthesis. * denotes new release.</p>
<p>&quot;Breakdown&quot; and &quot;The Saint&quot; are released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Austin Powers: International Man of Mystery&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, owned by Time Warner Inc.. Time Warner's Warner Bros. released &quot;Murder at 1600.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Volcano&quot; released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Liar Liar&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd..</p>
<p>&quot;Romy and Michele's High School Reunion&quot; and &quot;Grosse Pointe Blank&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co.</p>
<p>&quot;Anaconda&quot; is released by Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Warriors of Virtue&quot; is released by MGM, which is owned by Kirk Kerkorian and Australia's Seven Network Ltd.</p>
</text>
